From: gfx803_compat_graph C1b source audit <no-reply@example.invalid>
Subject: [RFC PATCH] drm/amdkfd: handle CPSCH startup queue execution errors outside reset

This is an RFC for inspection and kernel-build testing, not a
reviewed upstream fix. During GPU reset, the reset domain write lock
prevents execute_queues_cpsch() from acquiring its read trylock;
the old ignored -EIO at that call was not necessarily a failed
hardware queue. Explicitly skip queue execution under GPU reset.

Outside reset, surface a nonzero execute_queues_cpsch result and
unwind the startup allocations. Also clear sched_running on the
later detect-hang buffer allocation failure path, avoiding an
apparently running DQM whose resources were freed.

CAUTION: failure during an issued queue packet may leave hardware
state uncertain. This must be reviewed with upstream AMDGPU/KFD
maintainers before applying to a physical kernel. The offline C1b
model proves only the intended control-flow contract.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.c
@@ -2117,9 +2117,19 @@ static int start_cpsch(struct device_queue_manager *dqm)
 	/* clear hang status when driver try to start the hw scheduler */
 	dqm->sched_running = true;
 
 	if (!dqm->dev->kfd->shared_resources.enable_mes) {
 		if (pm_config_dequeue_wait_counts(&dqm->packet_mgr,
 				KFD_DEQUEUE_WAIT_INIT, 0 /* unused */))
 			dev_err(dev, "Setting optimized dequeue wait failed. Using default values\n");
-		execute_queues_cpsch(dqm, KFD_UNMAP_QUEUES_FILTER_DYNAMIC_QUEUES, 0, USE_DEFAULT_GRACE_PERIOD);
+		/*
+		 * GPU reset holds the reset-domain write semaphore: executing
+		 * queues here would fail its read trylock with -EIO.
+		 */
+		if (!amdgpu_in_reset(adev)) {
+			retval = execute_queues_cpsch(dqm,
+				KFD_UNMAP_QUEUES_FILTER_DYNAMIC_QUEUES,
+				0, USE_DEFAULT_GRACE_PERIOD);
+			if (retval)
+				goto fail_detect_hang_buffer;
+		}
 	}
@@ -2145,6 +2155,7 @@ static int start_cpsch(struct device_queue_manager *dqm)
 
 	return 0;
 fail_detect_hang_buffer:
+	dqm->sched_running = false;
 	kfd_gtt_sa_free(dqm->dev, dqm->fence_mem);
 fail_allocate_vidmem:
 fail_set_sched_resources:
-- 
